1
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:03,838
Hey, you guys.

2
00:00:03,879 --> 00:00:04,588
Hey.

3
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,756
Hey. What are you doing?

4
00:00:05,798 --> 00:00:07,549
Oh, figuring out
our wedding plans.

5
00:00:07,591 --> 00:00:09,468
That's funny. We were
doing the same thing.
Yeah.

6
00:00:11,553 --> 00:00:12,847
It's really crazy.

7
00:00:12,888 --> 00:00:14,055
The hall,

8
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:15,432
the dress, the food--

9
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:18,101
I-I had no idea
how expensive this stuff was.

10
00:00:18,143 --> 00:00:19,645
Yeah, it's really pricey.

11
00:00:19,687 --> 00:00:21,062
I mean, I freaked
when I first heard the numbers.

12
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:22,606
So what did you two
do about it?

13
00:00:22,648 --> 00:00:24,023
It's pretty simple actually.

14
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:26,318
I came up with a couple
cost-cutting solutions,

15
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,362
wrote out a list, and Monica
told me to go to hell.

16
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,573
ROSS:
There is no way
around it.

17
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:32,867
Pheebs, you're just going
have to accept the fact

18
00:00:32,908 --> 00:00:34,618
that this is going to
cost you a lot of money.

19
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:38,288
I heard the weddings are like
a $40-billion-a-year industry.

20
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:40,541
Yeah, and I'm responsible
for just like half of that.

21
00:00:42,668 --> 00:00:44,920
But, really, it does
seem like this money

22
00:00:44,962 --> 00:00:46,463
could be put
to better use.

23
00:00:46,505 --> 00:00:47,464
Are you serious?

24
00:00:47,506 --> 00:00:48,716
Yeah. Now,
how would you feel

25
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,258
if we gave
all the wedding money

26
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:53,721
to charity, and-and we just
got married at City Hall?

27
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:56,390
I figured it would make me
want to marry you even more.

28
00:00:58,017 --> 00:00:59,685
I've got to say,
you guys,

29
00:00:59,727 --> 00:01:02,229
that's, that's
an incredible gesture.

30
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,398
Maybe you'd do that
next time you get married.

31
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:07,568
No, no, no.

32
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:10,362
The next time it's going
to be Hawaii at sunset.

33
00:01:10,404 --> 00:01:12,740
But maybe the time after that.

34
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:17,118
Captioning sponsored by
WARNER BROS. TELEVISION

35
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:19,246
and NBC

36
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:24,167
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

37
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:26,921
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

38
00:01:26,962 --> 00:01:29,006
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

39
00:01:29,048 --> 00:01:34,093
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

40
00:01:34,135 --> 00:01:36,555
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

41
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:38,933
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

42
00:01:38,974 --> 00:01:42,728
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

43
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:48,525
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

44
00:01:53,405 --> 00:01:54,364
Hey.

45
00:01:54,406 --> 00:01:55,365
Hey.
Hey.

46
00:01:55,407 --> 00:01:56,867
What's going on?

47
00:01:56,909 --> 00:01:58,535
Our adoption social worker's
coming by today,

48
00:01:58,577 --> 00:02:00,161
so we're cleaning the apartment.

49
00:02:00,203 --> 00:02:02,539
"We"?

50
00:02:02,581 --> 00:02:04,458
You know
you don't want me to help.

51
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:06,627
You can't have it both ways.

52
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:09,128
Hey, is this the
person who decides

53
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:10,881
whether or not you get a baby?

54
00:02:10,923 --> 00:02:12,091
Kind of. She's coming by

55
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:13,801
to interview us
and see where we live.

56
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:15,385
And it has to go perfectly

57
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:17,096
because if she doesn't like
something about us,

58
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:19,098
she can keep us off every
adoption list in the state.

59
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:20,265
Hey, maybe
I should stop by.

60
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:22,059
She could be a soap opera fan.

61
00:02:22,101 --> 00:02:25,437
It's very impressive when the
little people know a celebrity.

62
00:02:26,814 --> 00:02:28,398
Little people?

63
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,900
Celebrity.

64
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:33,445
Okay, so I think
I'm just about done here,

65
00:02:33,487 --> 00:02:36,239
unless you have any bad stuff
hidden somewhere,

66
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:38,408
like porn or cigarettes?

67
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:40,911
What?!

68
00:02:40,953 --> 00:02:42,287
No!

69
00:02:42,329 --> 00:02:44,790
Chandler?

70
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:49,377
I don't, and I'm offended
by the insinuation.

71
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:50,671
Okay.

72
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:53,298
So there's not a magazine
under the couch?

73
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:56,384
Or a pack of cigarettes taped
to the back of a toilet tank?

74
00:02:56,426 --> 00:02:59,220
Or a filthy video
in the VCR?

75
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:02,099
I'll admit to
the cigarettes
and the magazine,

76
00:03:02,141 --> 00:03:03,809
but that tape is not mine.

77
00:03:03,851 --> 00:03:05,268
Well, it isn't mine.

78
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:07,312
Oh, I guess we'll never know
whose it is.

79
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:16,864
May I help you?

80
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:18,699
Yes. We're here
to make a rather

81
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,617
sizable donation
to the children.

82
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:23,411
Well, any contribution large
or small is always appreciated.

83
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:25,330
Well, I think you're
going to appreciate

84
00:03:25,372 --> 00:03:27,332
the crap out of this one.

85
00:03:27,374 --> 00:03:28,917
Well, this is very generous.

86
00:03:28,959 --> 00:03:30,627
And we don't want
any recognition.

87
00:03:30,669 --> 00:03:32,171
This is completely anonymous.

88
00:03:32,211 --> 00:03:33,463
Completely anonymous.

89
00:03:33,505 --> 00:03:34,965
From two kind strangers.

90
00:03:35,007 --> 00:03:38,093
Mr. X and Phoebe Buffay.

91
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:41,180
Oh, if you like, we can
include your names
in our newsletter.

92
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,181
Not necessary.

93
00:03:42,221 --> 00:03:44,307
Buffay is spelled B-U-F-F-A-Y.

94
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:49,188
And X is spelled...
Mike Hannigan.

95
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:52,149
All right, well, on behalf
of the children,

96
00:03:52,191 --> 00:03:53,358
thank you both very much.

97
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,110
Sure. I'm so glad
we did this.

98
00:03:55,152 --> 00:03:56,153
It feels so good.

99
00:03:56,195 --> 00:03:57,571
It does, it feels
really good.

100
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:58,613
Oh, look,

101
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:00,657
and we get these
free T-shirts!

102
00:04:00,699 --> 00:04:03,493
Actually, that's the shirt
I wore to the gym.

103
00:04:03,535 --> 00:04:06,038
Mm, it's moist.

104
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:09,917
Rach.
Hi!

105
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:11,334
Emma will be up in a minute.

106
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:12,836
Oh, good.

107
00:04:12,878 --> 00:04:15,463
Oh, hey, Ross, listen, I heard
about you and Charlie.

108
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:16,757
I'm really sorry.

109
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,383
Aw, that's okay.
I'm sure there are

110
00:04:18,425 --> 00:04:20,802
tons of other beautiful
paleontologists out there.

111
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:21,720
Absolutely.

112
00:04:21,762 --> 00:04:23,471
There was one! She's it!

113
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:27,142
All the rest look like they
should live under a bridge!

114
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:30,938
So, uh, what are you
going to do today?

115
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:33,857
Oh, I was thinking of taking
Emma to the playground.

116
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:36,568
Oh, my God. What?

117
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:39,446
Like I said, I was thinking

118
00:04:39,487 --> 00:04:42,741
of taking Emma to the Museum
of Knives and Fire.

119
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:47,287
Okay, look, Ross,
I do not

120
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:51,041
want Emma going
to the playground.

121
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:54,962
Because...

122
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:56,588
All right, well,
if you must know,

123
00:04:56,630 --> 00:05:03,137
I had a traumatic swing incident
when I was little.

124
00:05:03,178 --> 00:05:04,721
Seriously?

125
00:05:04,763 --> 00:05:06,723
Yes. I was four years old,

126
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:09,017
and I was on the swing,
and then all of a sudden,

127
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:11,979
my hair got tangled
in the chain...

128
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:15,356
And to get me out,
my mom had to,

129
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:17,901
had to cut a big
chunk of my hair.

130
00:05:19,903 --> 00:05:22,072
( choked up ):
And it was uneven for weeks.

131
00:05:25,617 --> 00:05:27,077
( sniffling )

132
00:05:28,912 --> 00:05:31,957
And you made it through that?

133
00:05:31,999 --> 00:05:35,043
I wonder who's going
to play you in the movie.

134
00:05:37,087 --> 00:05:39,047
Okay, fine, you can
make fun of me,

135
00:05:39,089 --> 00:05:41,049
I do not want Emma going there.

136
00:05:41,091 --> 00:05:43,927
And I was thinking Claire Danes.

137
00:05:44,928 --> 00:05:47,388
Look, I'm sorry to hear
about your tragedy,

138
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,641
okay, but the swings
are perfectly safe.

139
00:05:49,683 --> 00:05:51,310
And besides,
Emma loves them.

140
00:05:51,350 --> 00:05:53,312
You know what? You should
come with us and you'll see.

141
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:56,481
Ross, those things go,
like, 40 miles an hour!

142
00:05:56,523 --> 00:05:59,109
Okay, when you're at this
moment, when you're at the top,

143
00:05:59,151 --> 00:06:00,568
when you just don't know

144
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:02,988
if you're going to
return back to Earth.

145
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:07,575
Space is filled with
orbiting children.

146
00:06:10,204 --> 00:06:12,831
Look, please, just...
just come on.

147
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:15,209
You know what? When you see
the look on Emma's face,

148
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:16,584
I swear, you won't regret it.

149
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:19,338
All right.

150
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:20,964
Good.

151
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:22,924
You know, you don't want
to be one of those mothers

152
00:06:22,966 --> 00:06:25,760
who pass on their irrational
fears to their children, do you?

153
00:06:25,802 --> 00:06:27,262
Irrational, huh?

154
00:06:27,304 --> 00:06:29,097
All right, well, I'll remember
that the next time

155
00:06:29,139 --> 00:06:31,266
you freak out about a spider
in your apartment.

156
00:06:31,308 --> 00:06:33,101
Oh, yeah, that's the same.

157
00:06:33,143 --> 00:06:35,729
I'm sure there are 30 different
species of poisonous swings.

158
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:39,316
( knock at door )

159
00:06:39,358 --> 00:06:42,110
Oh, my God,
the adoption lady's early.

160
00:06:42,152 --> 00:06:43,444
Okay, okay.

161
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:45,446
Here we go,
here we go.
Okay.

162
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:47,324
Stand up straight.

163
00:06:47,366 --> 00:06:48,700
Big smile.

164
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:53,330
Hello. Is this
the Creepy residence?

165
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,415
We're waiting for
the adoption lady.

166
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:58,126
But hey, I'm glad you're here.

167
00:06:58,168 --> 00:07:00,795
I was cleaning this morning,
and I found this.

168
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:03,965
Now, I don't know
if you want to use it, but...

169
00:07:04,007 --> 00:07:07,219
Oh, this is
so sweet of you.

170
00:07:07,261 --> 00:07:09,304
Oh, but you know what?
I won't be needing a veil.

171
00:07:09,346 --> 00:07:11,181
I actually won't be
wearing a dress at all.

172
00:07:11,223 --> 00:07:14,017
I told you, I am not coming
to a naked wedding.

173
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:15,435
No, no, no,

174
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:17,104
we're just... we're not
having a big reception.

175
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:19,147
We took the money we're gonna
spend on the wedding,

176
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:20,815
and we donated it
to a children's charity.

177
00:07:20,857 --> 00:07:22,692
That's crazy!

178
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:26,196
I'm sorry. I just...

179
00:07:26,238 --> 00:07:28,990
I can't imagine giving up
my one wedding day like that.

180
00:07:29,032 --> 00:07:30,658
Yeah, well, we're different,
you know.

181
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,493
I don't care about
having a huge party.

182
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:34,579
This is really
nice for you,

183
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:36,790
but, oh, please,
I put this on

184
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:38,666
and ugh, I just look like...

185
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:41,044
well, radiant.

186
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:44,005
All right, but who cares?

187
00:07:44,047 --> 00:07:47,008
You know, I don't need
a pretty veil and a fancy dress.

188
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:49,844
That's right, you're making
a commitment and, you know,

189
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:52,513
that's the same whether
you do it at the Plaza or...

190
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:54,015
Where are you going to do it?

191
00:07:54,057 --> 00:07:54,891
City Hall.

192
00:07:54,933 --> 00:07:55,892
Oh!

193
00:07:55,934 --> 00:08:00,021
Oh, that sounds nice.

194
00:08:00,063 --> 00:08:02,023
Well, I was just there
for jury duty.

195
00:08:02,065 --> 00:08:04,109
They really spruced
that place up.

196
00:08:04,151 --> 00:08:05,610
Okay. No, it's okay.

197
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:07,237
It's okay, it's okay.

198
00:08:07,279 --> 00:08:08,696
I made my decision.

199
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:11,866
What I really want
is a great big wedding.

200
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:13,994
Yay!

201
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:16,746
But you already gave
all the money to charity.

202
00:08:16,788 --> 00:08:18,623
Well, just ask for it back.

203
00:08:18,665 --> 00:08:21,251
I don't think you can do that.

204
00:08:21,293 --> 00:08:22,252
Why not?

205
00:08:22,294 --> 00:08:23,753
This is her wedding day.

206
00:08:23,795 --> 00:08:26,714
That's way more important
than some stupid kids.

207
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:31,428
That's sweet, honey, but save
something for the adoption lady.

208
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,184
RACHEL:
Okay.

209
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:38,226
Here we go.

210
00:08:38,268 --> 00:08:39,853
All right, okay,
be careful.

211
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:41,520
Okay.
Be careful.

212
00:08:41,562 --> 00:08:42,605
Watch her hair.

213
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:44,399
Watch her hair!

214
00:08:44,441 --> 00:08:47,068
Rach, she's got,
like, three hairs.

215
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:48,445
I know.

216
00:08:48,487 --> 00:08:50,405
I know, but they're
just so beautiful.

217
00:08:50,447 --> 00:08:53,574
Oh, my God, I just
pulled one out!

218
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:55,369
I promise you,
she's safe, okay?

219
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:57,662
Now watch. Watch how
much she loves this.

220
00:08:57,704 --> 00:08:59,247
Okay, okay.
Are you ready,
sweetie?

221
00:08:59,289 --> 00:09:00,290
Here we go.

222
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,418
Okay, careful.

223
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:05,170
( cooing )
'Kay.

224
00:09:05,212 --> 00:09:06,505
( cooing )
Oh.

225
00:09:06,545 --> 00:09:09,299
( cooing )
Oh!

226
00:09:09,341 --> 00:09:11,301
She's smiling.

227
00:09:11,343 --> 00:09:13,928
Oh, look at that!
She just likes it.

228
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:15,263
See? I told you.

229
00:09:15,305 --> 00:09:17,140
Oh... oh.

230
00:09:17,182 --> 00:09:18,141
Oh!

231
00:09:18,183 --> 00:09:20,685
( giggling )

232
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:22,103
Oh, my God!

233
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:24,689
Look at her, she's
a little daredevil!

234
00:09:24,731 --> 00:09:27,108
Oh, God, oh,
let me push.
Can I push?

235
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:28,485
Oh, absolutely.
Okay.

236
00:09:28,527 --> 00:09:30,529
Oh, gosh.

237
00:09:30,569 --> 00:09:31,863
Okay, get the camera.

238
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:33,031
It's in the diaper bag.

239
00:09:33,073 --> 00:09:34,366
Okay.

240
00:09:34,408 --> 00:09:35,534
See?

241
00:09:35,574 --> 00:09:36,951
Scared of the swings.

242
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:38,495
I bet you'll feel pretty silly.

243
00:09:38,537 --> 00:09:40,539
( screams )
( yells )

244
00:09:43,208 --> 00:09:45,835
We're seriously asking
for the money back?

245
00:09:45,877 --> 00:09:47,337
It's for our
wedding day.

246
00:09:47,379 --> 00:09:49,339
All right, now, is this
guy gay or straight?

247
00:09:49,381 --> 00:09:51,799
'Cause one of us's gonna
have to start flirting.

248
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:55,303
Wow! You're here to make
another donation the same day?

249
00:09:55,345 --> 00:09:57,597
I don't think that's
ever happened before.

250
00:09:57,638 --> 00:09:58,973
Gay. Go.

251
00:10:02,436 --> 00:10:04,271
Oh, my God,
I love your shirt.

252
00:10:05,439 --> 00:10:06,565
All right.

253
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:08,525
The donation we made earlier,

254
00:10:08,567 --> 00:10:11,319
um, well, we... we want,
we want it back.

255
00:10:11,361 --> 00:10:13,654
Excuse me?

256
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:15,490
Yeah, see, okay, that
money was for, um,

257
00:10:15,532 --> 00:10:17,617
a big wedding that we
thought we didn't want.

258
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:19,369
But it turns out we do.

259
00:10:19,411 --> 00:10:22,539
So, you're asking us to refund
your donation to the children?

260
00:10:22,581 --> 00:10:24,416
Yeah.

261
00:10:25,792 --> 00:10:27,794
This feels really good.

262
00:10:31,256 --> 00:10:33,341
Yeah, I'm sor... I'm sorry,
I am, but you know,

263
00:10:33,383 --> 00:10:35,385
this wedding's just
really important to me.

264
00:10:35,427 --> 00:10:37,220
It's none of my business.

265
00:10:37,262 --> 00:10:39,013
Besides, this is
probably a good thing.

266
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,932
We've really been spoiling
the children,

267
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:44,018
what with all the food
and warm clothing.

268
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:46,020
That's not fair.

269
00:10:46,062 --> 00:10:49,274
A person's wedding is important,
and especially to me.

270
00:10:49,316 --> 00:10:52,193
Okay? I-I didn't have
a graduation party

271
00:10:52,235 --> 00:10:53,778
and I didn't go to prom.

272
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:57,491
And I spent my sweet 16
being chased around a tire yard

273
00:10:57,532 --> 00:11:00,034
by an... escaped mental patient

274
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:03,079
who, in his own words,
wanted to kill me or whatever.

275
00:11:05,415 --> 00:11:07,626
So, I deserve
a real celebration,

276
00:11:07,666 --> 00:11:10,670
and-and-and I'm not gonna
let some sweaty little man

277
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:12,213
make me feel
badly about it.

278
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:18,886
She could have been talking
about either one of us.

279
00:11:22,474 --> 00:11:24,058
( knock at door )

280
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:26,520
Hi. I'm Laura.

281
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:28,480
I'm here for your
adoption interview.

282
00:11:28,522 --> 00:11:29,772
Hi. I'm Monica.

283
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:31,149
And this is Chandler.

284
00:11:31,191 --> 00:11:32,651
Hi.
Please come in.

285
00:11:32,691 --> 00:11:33,776
Thank you.

286
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:35,153
Would you like
something to drink?

287
00:11:35,195 --> 00:11:36,321
Oh, water
would be fine.

288
00:11:36,363 --> 00:11:37,405
Okay, great.

289
00:11:37,447 --> 00:11:39,366
We're so glad
that you're here.

290
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:42,577
We're really excited about
getting this process started.

291
00:11:42,619 --> 00:11:43,744
Because we love kids.

292
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:45,288
Love 'em to death.

293
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:47,290
Well, not actually to death.

294
00:11:47,332 --> 00:11:49,042
That's just a figure of speech.

295
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:51,085
We love kids
the appropriate amount.

296
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:55,089
As allowed by law.

297
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:58,552
Your place is just lovely.

298
00:11:58,593 --> 00:12:00,261
Oh, thank you.

299
00:12:00,303 --> 00:12:03,390
Yes, this building does have
a wholesome family feel to it.

300
00:12:03,431 --> 00:12:05,642
You know, I-I feel like
I've been here before.

301
00:12:05,684 --> 00:12:07,977
Are any other couples
in the building adopting?

302
00:12:08,019 --> 00:12:10,063
Is that-that couple
on the first floor?

303
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:12,232
Because we should get a baby
before them.

304
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:14,609
Yeah, that guy tried
to sell me drugs!

305
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:17,736
But other than that,
wholesome...

306
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:18,779
wholesome building.

307
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:21,740
Oh...

308
00:12:21,782 --> 00:12:23,117
What?

309
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:26,246
I just realized why
I remember this place.

310
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:27,997
Really? What is it?
Oh, it's nothing.

311
00:12:28,039 --> 00:12:30,417
I went on a date with a guy
who lived in this building.

312
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:31,792
It didn't end very well.

313
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:35,505
That wouldn't by any chance
be Joey Tribbiani?

314
00:12:35,547 --> 00:12:36,423
Yes!

315
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:38,383
Of course it was.

316
00:12:39,384 --> 00:12:41,094
Yeah, we had
a really great night

317
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:43,762
and in the morning, he promised
he would call me and he didn't.

318
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:45,515
Rat bastard!

319
00:12:47,350 --> 00:12:48,685
So you're not friends with him?

320
00:12:48,727 --> 00:12:49,686
Oh, God, no!

321
00:12:49,728 --> 00:12:51,396
Nope. No, no, no.
No.

322
00:12:51,438 --> 00:12:53,147
No, nope.
Nope.

323
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:54,773
No, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no.
No, no, no.

324
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:56,443
No!

325
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:57,652
No.

326
00:12:58,986 --> 00:13:02,365
Well, I'm sorry I brought it up.

327
00:13:02,407 --> 00:13:05,201
So, are either one of you
planning on staying at home?

328
00:13:05,243 --> 00:13:06,202
( knock at door )

329
00:13:06,244 --> 00:13:07,662
JOEY:
Hello?!

330
00:13:07,704 --> 00:13:08,996
Anybody in there?

331
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:10,624
Order a celebrity?

332
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:11,832
Ow!

333
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:15,712
Wh-What's that?

334
00:13:15,754 --> 00:13:18,632
Oh, it's just some crazy guy
who roams the halls here.

335
00:13:18,673 --> 00:13:21,175
He's great with kids, though.

336
00:13:27,474 --> 00:13:29,100
Oh, God, Ross!

337
00:13:29,142 --> 00:13:30,393
Oh, my God!
Are you okay?

338
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:32,646
Son of a bitch!

339
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:39,277
Oh, relax.
I didn't say the F-word!

340
00:13:41,154 --> 00:13:42,196
Ross, see?

341
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,157
I told you those
swings are evil!

342
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:45,492
All right,
that is it.

343
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:46,867
That is the last time

344
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:48,202
Emma is getting on
one of those things

345
00:13:48,244 --> 00:13:49,162
for her entire life.

346
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,288
No! No, no, no, no.

347
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:52,290
Okay, it wasn't
the swing's fault.

348
00:13:52,332 --> 00:13:54,208
It was my fault...
and kind of

349
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:56,043
that kid's fault.

350
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:59,297
Who is still laughing.
Nice.

351
00:13:59,339 --> 00:14:00,507
Ross, come on, please.

352
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:01,591
Could we just get
out of here

353
00:14:01,633 --> 00:14:03,009
before somebody else
gets hurt?

354
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:04,927
No, wait-- okay, okay,
I have an idea.

355
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:07,054
I want you to get
on the swing, okay,

356
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:10,057
and you'll see that
there's nothing
to be afraid of.

357
00:14:12,602 --> 00:14:15,480
I know what this
is all about.

358
00:14:15,522 --> 00:14:17,691
You've always been
jealous of my hair.

359
00:14:19,275 --> 00:14:21,361
Look, I just think
you're an adult, okay?

360
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:23,530
And you should get over
your silly fears.

361
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:25,281
All right, fine.
I'll do it.

362
00:14:25,323 --> 00:14:27,200
Good.
If you hold a spider.

363
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:29,118
What?! Where?! Where?!

364
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:32,205
If you hold a spider.

365
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:34,081
I know.

366
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:36,125
( groans )

367
00:14:40,547 --> 00:14:42,674
JOEY:
Guys! Is everything okay?

368
00:14:42,716 --> 00:14:43,758
It's me, Joey!

369
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,218
( screams )

370
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:48,471
Aah... gumption!

371
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:51,516
What's going on?

372
00:14:51,558 --> 00:14:54,394
Oh, just like I said,
that crazy...

373
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:56,062
Bert...

374
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:57,230
roaming the halls.

375
00:14:57,271 --> 00:14:58,897
( pounding )
Guys!

376
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:01,401
Keep on roaming, Bert!

377
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:04,362
We don't want
any crazy today!

378
00:15:04,404 --> 00:15:05,613
JOEY:
What's going on?

379
00:15:05,655 --> 00:15:07,281
We'll talk to you later,
Bert.

380
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:08,783
Everything's fine!

381
00:15:08,825 --> 00:15:12,078
Everything doesn't sound fine.

382
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:14,581
Is he all right,
out there by himself?

383
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:15,915
Oh, yeah.
He has a caretaker.

384
00:15:15,956 --> 00:15:17,916
His older brother...

385
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:19,377
Ernie.

386
00:15:21,796 --> 00:15:23,506
Bert and Ernie.

387
00:15:23,548 --> 00:15:25,550
You can't make this stuff up.

388
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:30,263
You never told me about
that guy and your Sweet 16.

389
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:32,223
Ugh! I'm sorry about that.

390
00:15:32,265 --> 00:15:33,767
Oh, it ended okay.

391
00:15:33,808 --> 00:15:35,435
One of my friends
shot him.

392
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:40,064
Well, hey, at least you're
getting a proper wedding.

393
00:15:40,106 --> 00:15:41,441
I mean, you really
deserve that.

394
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:42,983
Yeah, I really do.

395
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,402
You know, I had nothing
growing up.

396
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:49,574
Just like the kids
I took the money from.

397
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:51,075
No.

398
00:15:51,117 --> 00:15:53,327
No, no, I see
where this is going.

399
00:15:53,369 --> 00:15:55,204
Don't make me
go back there.

400
00:15:55,246 --> 00:15:58,666
Look, I can't have a wedding
with this money now.

401
00:15:58,708 --> 00:16:00,293
It's tainted.

402
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:03,463
All right, fine.
We'll give the money back.

403
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:05,423
And if that guy at the charity
gives us a hard time,

404
00:16:05,465 --> 00:16:09,051
my friend hasn't shot anyone
in a really long time.

405
00:16:10,678 --> 00:16:12,430
Well, I must say
this seems like

406
00:16:12,472 --> 00:16:14,432
a lovely environment
to raise a child in.

407
00:16:14,474 --> 00:16:16,392
Oh, by the way, you
are more than welcome

408
00:16:16,434 --> 00:16:17,644
to look under any
of the furniture,

409
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:19,395
because, believe me,

410
00:16:19,437 --> 00:16:21,147
you won't find any
porn or cigarettes
under there.

411
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:22,523
Oh, thanks.

412
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:24,150
Well, actually,
before we look around,

413
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:25,860
let me make sure I have
everything I need up to here.

414
00:16:31,866 --> 00:16:34,076
Why don't I show you
the baby's room?

415
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:40,792
What the hell
are you doing?

416
00:16:40,834 --> 00:16:41,876
Well, you wouldn't
let me in,

417
00:16:41,918 --> 00:16:43,043
so I thought
you were in trouble!

418
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:44,378
Well, we're not!

419
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:45,630
But you called me Bert!

420
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,509
That's our code word
for "danger."

421
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:52,428
We don't have a code word.

422
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,388
We don't?!

423
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:56,516
We really should.

424
00:16:56,557 --> 00:17:00,603
From now on, "Bert" will be
our code word for danger.

425
00:17:00,645 --> 00:17:02,271
So that was the
baby's room...

426
00:17:04,691 --> 00:17:06,359
Uh, what room
should we see next?

427
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,194
Any room that isn't
behind this couch.

428
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:11,322
( forced laughter )

429
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:12,699
Some people don't get him,

430
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,742
but I think
he's really funny.

431
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:24,836
I did not care
for that.

432
00:17:24,878 --> 00:17:27,046
You have to get
out of here.

433
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:28,422
You slept with
our social worker,

434
00:17:28,464 --> 00:17:29,841
and you never
called her back,

435
00:17:29,883 --> 00:17:31,968
and she is still
pissed, so she
can't see you.

436
00:17:32,010 --> 00:17:33,427
Oh, okay, okay, okay.

437
00:17:35,805 --> 00:17:37,097
What?!

438
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:38,391
I forgot my bat.

439
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:44,271
Oh, my God!

440
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:45,732
And for the last time,

441
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:48,735
we do not want to be
friends with you!

442
00:17:50,945 --> 00:17:52,780
And we don't want
to buy your bat!

443
00:17:55,366 --> 00:17:57,117
What are you doing here?

444
00:17:57,159 --> 00:17:59,746
Bert, Bert, Bert,
Bert...

445
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:04,959
Are you friends with him?

446
00:18:05,001 --> 00:18:07,587
I can explain.

447
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:09,964
Joey?

448
00:18:10,006 --> 00:18:11,799
Uh, okay, uh...

449
00:18:14,176 --> 00:18:19,223
Oh, yeah... you have got
some nerve coming back here.

450
00:18:20,934 --> 00:18:22,476
I can't believe
you never called me.

451
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:23,686
Excuse me?!

452
00:18:23,728 --> 00:18:24,896
Oh! Yeah!

453
00:18:24,938 --> 00:18:26,522
Probably don't even
remember my name!

454
00:18:26,564 --> 00:18:28,315
It's Joey, by the way.

455
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:29,609
And don't bother
telling me yours,

456
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:32,570
because I totally remember it...
lady.

457
00:18:34,405 --> 00:18:35,615
Yeah.

458
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:37,157
I waited weeks
for you to call me!

459
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:39,410
I gave you my number;
you never called me.

460
00:18:39,452 --> 00:18:41,621
Don't try to turn this around
on me, okay?

461
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:44,331
I am not some... kind of...

462
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:48,377
social work, okay,
that you can just... do.

463
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:54,008
Well, I'm pretty sure
I gave you my number.

464
00:18:54,050 --> 00:18:55,175
Really?

465
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:56,803
Think about it.
Come on.

466
00:18:56,844 --> 00:18:59,055
You're a beautiful woman,
smart,

467
00:18:59,097 --> 00:19:00,431
funny.

468
00:19:00,473 --> 00:19:04,102
We had a really
good time, huh?

469
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:07,105
If I had your number,
why wouldn't I call you?

470
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:08,856
I don't know.

471
00:19:11,067 --> 00:19:13,235
Well, maybe I'm wrong.
I'm sorry.

472
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:16,614
No, no, hey, no.
Too late for apologies, okay?

473
00:19:16,656 --> 00:19:18,407
You broke my heart.

474
00:19:18,449 --> 00:19:20,868
You know how many women I had
to sleep with to get over you?

475
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:25,915
Joey, wait!

476
00:19:25,957 --> 00:19:27,416
No!

477
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:29,293
I waited a long time.
I can't wait anymore.

478
00:19:33,756 --> 00:19:35,382
I'm sorry that
you had to see that.

479
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:36,717
I'm so embarrassed.

480
00:19:36,759 --> 00:19:38,260
Oh, that's really okay.

481
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:40,262
Yeah, and we
totally understand.

482
00:19:40,304 --> 00:19:41,889
Dating is hard!

483
00:19:41,931 --> 00:19:43,933
Boy, you people
are nice.

484
00:19:43,975 --> 00:19:45,476
( laughs )

485
00:19:45,518 --> 00:19:47,478
And I've got to say...

486
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:50,314
I think you're going to make
excellent parents.

487
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:56,320
Laura!

488
00:19:58,948 --> 00:20:00,741
( door slams )

489
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:05,579
We're back.

490
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:07,498
Are you here
to take more money?

491
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:11,127
Because I think what you're
looking for is an ATM.

492
00:20:11,169 --> 00:20:13,713
No, no, we're here
to give the money back.

493
00:20:13,754 --> 00:20:15,756
Yeah, 'cause, you
know what, it's...

494
00:20:15,798 --> 00:20:18,051
it's all about the children.

495
00:20:18,092 --> 00:20:19,426
Although...

496
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:20,970
it's also about the wedding.

497
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:23,597
Ugh. All right. Here.

498
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,183
No. Oh, God! Oh...

499
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:29,062
If I haven't said so already,
sir-- congratulations.

500
00:20:29,103 --> 00:20:31,064
Okay, look, enough.
All right?

501
00:20:31,105 --> 00:20:33,232
I'm stepping in.
I'm putting my foot down.

502
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:35,735
As your future husband,
I'm going to make this
decision for us.

503
00:20:35,776 --> 00:20:38,278
Okay.

504
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:41,199
W-What do you think
we should do?

505
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:43,910
You know what?
It's not your decision anymore.

506
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:44,994
What?!
On behalf

507
00:20:45,036 --> 00:20:46,120
of the children
of New York,

508
00:20:46,162 --> 00:20:48,122
I reject your money.

509
00:20:48,164 --> 00:20:50,457
B-But we're giving you this.

510
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:51,918
Yeah, and I'm giving it
back to you.

511
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,920
Come on.
Consider it a contribution.

512
00:20:56,130 --> 00:20:58,591
Well, this is
very generous.

513
00:20:58,632 --> 00:21:00,593
Please, take the check.

514
00:21:00,634 --> 00:21:03,637
Go have a great wedding
and a wonderful life together.

515
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:05,223
Well, I mean,
it sounds good to me.

516
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:06,807
And that way, we can save up,
come back in a few years,

517
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:08,809
and make an even bigger
donation.
Absolutely.

518
00:21:08,851 --> 00:21:10,770
And when you do,
make sure you ask for Brian.

519
00:21:10,811 --> 00:21:11,478
Oh, is that you?

520
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:12,230
No.

521
00:21:14,857 --> 00:21:17,275
( phone rings )

522
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:19,946
Hello.

523
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:22,782
Oh, hi.

524
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:24,324
Oh, my God!

525
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:25,534
Really?

526
00:21:25,576 --> 00:21:26,994
I can't wait to
tell Chandler.

527
00:21:27,036 --> 00:21:28,871
Okay. Good-bye.

528
00:21:28,913 --> 00:21:30,539
Wrong number?

529
00:21:30,581 --> 00:21:32,332
That was Laura.

530
00:21:32,374 --> 00:21:34,627
She gave us
a great report

531
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:36,336
and we are officially
on the waiting list.

532
00:21:36,378 --> 00:21:38,214
That's great!
Now we just have
to wait for a call

533
00:21:38,256 --> 00:21:41,508
and someone tells
us there's a baby
waiting for us.

534
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:43,469
Oh!
Aw...

535
00:21:45,471 --> 00:21:49,100
( phone ringing )

536
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:56,356
Hello?

537
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:58,692
Have you seen Joey's bat?

538
00:22:00,194 --> 00:22:03,156
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

539
00:22:05,658 --> 00:22:07,576
Okay. I got a spider.

540
00:22:07,618 --> 00:22:10,704
There were two.
I picked the bigger one.

541
00:22:10,746 --> 00:22:13,331
Okay...
Okay.

542
00:22:15,168 --> 00:22:17,128
( gasps )

543
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:20,214
This feels perfectly normal.

544
00:22:20,256 --> 00:22:22,842
Okay, get on the swing.

545
00:22:25,678 --> 00:22:27,847
Okay...

546
00:22:27,888 --> 00:22:29,890
O... kay...

547
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:37,523
Okay.

548
00:22:39,399 --> 00:22:41,401
Oop. Okay.

549
00:22:43,029 --> 00:22:44,322
( whimpers )

550
00:22:44,362 --> 00:22:45,323
Oh!

551
00:22:45,363 --> 00:22:46,324
See?

552
00:22:46,364 --> 00:22:48,075
Oh, all right.
I can do this.

553
00:22:48,117 --> 00:22:49,076
There you go!

554
00:22:49,118 --> 00:22:50,703
Good for you!

555
00:22:50,744 --> 00:22:52,079
And you know what?

556
00:22:52,121 --> 00:22:53,455
I'm actually getting used
to this little guy.

557
00:22:53,497 --> 00:22:55,373
I don't really even
feel him in here anymore.

558
00:22:55,415 --> 00:22:56,458
That's 'cause he's
on your neck.

559
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:57,710
( shrieking )

560
00:22:57,751 --> 00:22:58,836
Oh, my God!

561
00:22:58,878 --> 00:23:00,838
Oh! Ross! Ross!

